    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d102">

                <pb facs="0099" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg85"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.00/4–1147: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Hanoi</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >O’Sullivan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanoi</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-04-11T08:00:00+08:00">April 11, 1947—8
                            a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>124. According French monitoring service, Radio Vietnam March 10 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">30?</hi>] reported that Ho Chi Minh, upon learning death
                    of Colonels <pb facs="0100" n="86" xml:id="pg86"/> Debes and Gufflet<anchor
                        n="77" xml:id="d102-f1"/> (previously said by Radio Vietnam to have been
                    shot down by VN anti-aircraft guns) declared: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“As French they were our friends, as soldiers they were brave, as
                            colonialists they were our opponents. But before God and humanity
                            everyone is a brother and equal. That is why I bow before their souls. I
                            deeply regret that men of valor such as they are sacrificed in this
                            fratricidal war. Otherwise they would have been very useful in common
                            work between France and Vietnam.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>This declaration continues tenor of remarks attributed by Radio Vietnam to Ho
                    since December 19. During that time remarks alleged to have originated with Ho
                    have never been directed against France but when critical to “reactionary
                    colonialists”.</p>
                <p>Repeat to Paris.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">O’Sullivan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d102-f1" n="77" xml:id="d102-f1-content">
                <p>Colonel Gufflet, chief of staff to General Jean Valluy, was killed in the same
                    plane crash as Colonel Debes on March 30.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
